- **Real GDP** collapsed dramatically from 67,440 in 1990 to a low of 18,658 in 1994 (a 72% decline), reflecting the severe post-Soviet economic crisis. It has since recovered steadily, surpassing the 1990 level by 2017 and reaching 91,438 in 2023.
